{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev_interior",
    "description": "Interior-only conservative finite-volume divergence of the TOTAL interface flux K du/dz - F on column_nonuniform_1d: L u[k] = ( (K[k+1] (u[k+1]-u[k])/(zc[k+1]-zc[k]) - F[k+1]) - (K[k] (u[k]-u[k-1])/(zc[k]-zc[k-1]) - F[k]) ) / dz[k] over k in [2, NLEV-1], with the coefficient K and the prescribed flux F both supplied AT THE INTERFACES (shape [lev_nodes]; node 1 is the surface, node k separates layers k-1 and k, node NLEV+1 is the model top). It is the interior stencil of stencils/varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_interior with the interface flux F subtracted inside the same difference, so the diffusive and the prescribed parts of the flux telescope together: sum_k dz[k] L u[k] over the interior equals the difference of the total flux across the two bounding interfaces. Match-less named template; rules/varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev wraps it with the two boundary layers. `zc` and `dz` are the consumer's free-name geometry observeds (grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm). Second-order in L2 on a smoothly stretched column (supraconvergent).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "op:varcoeff_laplacian",
      "order:2",
      "stencil_width:3"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev_interior": {
